# ── Glean .gitignore ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Principle: the repo is PUBLIC by default. Anything that must never be
# published is excluded here, so exclusion is enforced by the repo, not
# by remembering. See docs/ETHICS.md ("Data governance").

# ── Never publish: private planning + third-party copyrighted material ──
# planning docs, research PDFs, anything not for the world
_private/

# ── Never publish: real reconnaissance data ──
# Raw tool output and scan results about real infrastructure are sensitive
# even for domains you own. Commit only sanitised fixtures, deliberately.
raw/
# The one deliberate sanitised fixture this rule's comment allows for: the
# committed CI evaluation target (roadmap E3). RFC 2606 `example.com`,
# byte-identical copies of fixtures already in this repo, describing no real
# infrastructure. Without it `raw/` matches at every depth and CI silently
# evaluates a target with no captures at all -- which scored a *perfect*
# 1.000, because an empty graph has nothing to be unfaithful about.
# Re-including the directory itself is required, not optional: git will not
# descend into an excluded directory, so `!...raw/*.json` alone matches
# nothing.
!tests/fixtures/eval/**/raw/
# The public reproduction set (eval/public/). One target -- scanme.nmap.org,
# a host Nmap explicitly provides for public scanning -- so an outsider can
# actually run `glean eval` against real captures and a real human ranking
# rather than taking the numbers on trust. It names no private
# infrastructure: its crt.sh capture is empty and dnsx resolved only the
# scan target itself, both checked before committing.
#
# The private set in eval/scans/ stays excluded and remains the research
# evidence; this one demonstrates the method, not the result.
!eval/public/**/raw/
scans/
*.scan.json
targets.txt
targets.md
**/live-*.json

# ── Secrets / config ──
.env
*.key
config/*.local.*
**/secrets.*

# ── Python (for when development starts) ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# ── OS / editor noise ──
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
